{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1232, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nYou are given a sequence of integers A = (A_1, A_2, A_3).\r\nLet B = (B_1, B_2, B_3) be any permutation of A.\r\nDetermine whether it is possible that B_1 \\times B_2 = B_3.\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nA_1 A_2 A_3\n\nOutput\n\nIf it is possible that B_1 \\times B_2 = B_3, print Yes; otherwise, print No.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- All input values are integers.\n- 1 \\le A_1, A_2, A_3 \\le 100\n\nSample Input 1\n\n3 15 5\n\nSample Output 1\n\nYes\r\n\nHere, A=(3,15,5).\r\nBy rearranging it as B=(3,5,15), we can satisfy B_1 \\times B_2 = B_3.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n5 3 2\n\nSample Output 2\n\nNo\r\n\nNo permutation of B satisfies B_1 \\times B_2 = B_3.\n\n### Format: Read the inputs from stdin solve the problem and write the answer to stdout (do not directly test on the sample inputs). Enclose your code within delimiters as follows. Ensure that when the python program runs, it reads the inputs, runs the algorithm and writes output to STDOUT.\n```python\n# YOUR CODE HERE\n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1269, "char_start": 1244, "quote": "Input:\n3 15 5\nOutput:\nYes", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 1304, "char_start": 1281, "quote": "Input:\n5 3 2\nOutput:\nNo", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "bd088b0ed3baf861a5f7f529bb4c137443e544844b2e55a8563a3b193cc4ec15", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "b8769fb81daa531f5531135671ab4a5e91bf1ad3c17c0bec0ad0dc12b0fd6d00", "seq": 2}
